---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  article={{
    publishedTime: dates.published,
    modifiedTime: dates.modified,
    author: authorName(Astro.url.pathname),
    section: "Bedroom & Sleep",
    tags: [
      "best mattress protector",
      "best mattress protectors",
      "waterproof mattress protector",
      "mattress encasement",
      "bed bug mattress protector",
      "breathable mattress protector"
    ],
  }}
  jsonLd={schema}
>
  <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
      <div class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10" style="background-image: radial-gradient(circle at 20% 20%, #38BDF8 0, transparent 45%), radial-gradient(circle at 80% 60%, #FF4500 0, transparent 40%);"></div>
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-center gap-3 mb-6">
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#FF4500]/20 text-[#FF4500] text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-widest border border-[#FF4500]/30">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
          <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-green-500/10 text-green-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest border border-green-500/20">
            Buyer's Guide
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Mattress Protectors</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          A mattress protector is the cheapest insurance a bed can have. The right one keeps out sweat and spills without making noise or sleeping hot, and an encasement adds full coverage when bed bugs or allergens are a concern.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="#saferest-premium"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
          >
            See Our #1 Pick
          </a>
          <a
            href="#top-picks"
            class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
          >
            Jump to the Rankings
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-6 border-b border-gray-100 pb-8">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
          <AuthorAvatar size={48} />
          <div>
            <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Alex Rivers</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 uppercase tracking-widest">Home Improvement Editor</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="h-10 w-px bg-gray-200 hidden sm:block"></div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block">
          <p class="text-sm font-bold text-gray-900">Last Updated</p>
          <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">{dates.display}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="8.7k" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of Contents -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
      <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-black text-gray-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          In This Guide
        </h2>
        <nav class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2">
          <a href="#waterproof-breathable" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">1. Waterproof vs Breathable</a>
          <a href="#top-picks" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">2. The 6 Best, Ranked</a>
          <a href="#encasement-fitted" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">3. Encasement vs Fitted</a>
          <a href="#allergens-bed-bugs" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">4. Allergens and Bed Bugs</a>
          <a href="#noise" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">5. Noise</a>
          <a href="#washing" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">6. Washing</a>
          <a href="#who" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">7. Kids, Seniors and Pets</a>
          <a href="#verdict" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">8. Which to Buy</a>
          <a href="#mistakes" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">9. Common Mistakes</a>
          <a href="#faq" class="text-sm text-gray-600 hover:text-[#1E90FF] no-underline py-1 font-medium">10. FAQ</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Most people think about a mattress protector only after the first spill. By then the stain is in the foam and, with many mattresses, the warranty is gone. Choosing one is simpler than the shelf suggests once you know the two decisions that matter: how it handles liquid and air, and how much of the mattress it covers.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="waterproof-breathable" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Waterproof vs Breathable: You Can Have Both, Within Limits
          </h2>

          <p>
            Every mattress protector is a balance between keeping liquid out and letting air and moisture vapor through. A protector that blocks everything sleeps hot and crinkles. One that breathes freely lets spills reach the mattress. Modern protectors get close to both, and understanding how they do it makes the choice easier.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How a Waterproof Layer Works</h3>

          <p>
            Most waterproof protectors use a thin membrane, usually polyurethane or TPU, bonded to the underside of the top fabric. The membrane has pores small enough to stop liquid but large enough, the makers say, to let some water vapor through. That is why a modern protector feels far less sweaty than the vinyl covers of the past. Vinyl and PVC protectors still exist, mostly at the very bottom of the market, and are the ones to avoid.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Why Waterproofing Matters for Your Warranty</h3>

          <p>
            Many mattress makers void the warranty if the mattress is stained, and sweat alone will discolor a mattress over a few years. A waterproof protector is the cheapest way to keep a warranty valid, which is why many retailers suggest one with every new mattress. Our <a href="/best-mattress/">best mattress guide</a> covers what to look for in the warranty itself.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">Breathable, Non-Waterproof Protectors</h3>

          <p>
            Some protectors are cotton or wool with no membrane at all. They breathe best, but they only slow liquid down. They make sense for people who sleep very hot and are not worried about spills, though most households are better served by a breathable waterproof protector.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">The Top Fabric Changes the Feel</h3>

          <p>
            Terry cotton is absorbent and soft but adds a slight texture. Smooth polyester and bamboo viscose are thinner and feel closer to the sheet. On a memory foam mattress, a thin top keeps more of the contouring feel. The table compares the picks.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Product</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Type</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Key spec</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best for</th>
                  </tr>
